                <pb facs="0831" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.927/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Howell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-29T17:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 29—2:51
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Officially informed that antiquities law now prevailing will continue season
                    of 1923–24 permitting our museums to continue their work.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
